  "description": "Why I’m Staying Bullish, the stock ownership metric I pay attention to, and what is ahead for the market this week.",
  "body_html": "<p>Looking like a pretty decent start to the week in the Stock Market. Most of our stocks are pushing up this Monday morning. </p><p>Last week, I sensed some hopelessness amongst some individuals. I wish the stock market went up every single day, lots and lots. But that simply is not how it goes. We will have <em><strong>pull backs</strong></em>, <em><strong>consolidations,</strong></em> <strong>slow periods</strong>… but those periods are eventually met with <em><strong>reversals</strong></em>, <em><strong>breakouts </strong></em>and<em><strong> fast periods</strong></em>. So just because 1, or a few weeks, are not exactly thrilling to you… don’t run off. Good times always follow bad times!</p><div><hr></div><p>It is common for me to see in the comments section, particularly on TikTok:</p><p>“This insider was selling (insert ticker) shares!” or;</p><p>“That CEO was buying (insert ticker) like crazy!”</p><h4><em><strong>Individual</strong></em><strong> insider trading signals are usually useless!</strong></h4><p>It is especially bad when the news hits mainstream media, which is wrong in stock price direction far more often than it is right. </p><p>Normally, I ignore these headlines. </p><p>A more useful indication of stock price direction, is <strong>closely held shares.</strong> If I am deciding between 2 stocks, which one to buy, and all other variables are equal… I will <em><strong>select the stock that has a higher percentage of closely held shares</strong></em>. </p><p>You may recall, I recently reviewed Advanced Micro Devices, <span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;$AMD&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span> and Tesla, <span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;$TSLA&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span>. Amongst many variables, my analysis led my to summarize that Tesla is the better purchase in the longer term. One of those variables, is that 28.5% of the total shares, are still closely held… compared to only .51% for AMD.   </p><p>If there is some big news that hits, Tesla is more likely to have a supply shortage, driving stock price up. </p><div class=\"captioned-image-container\"><figure><div class=\"image-link image2\" data-component-name=\"Image2ToDOM\"><div class=\"image2-inset\"><picture><source type=\"image/webp\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HBmN!,w_424,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb462a257-e9a4-4957-a17b-b3e3c70f8b15_632x163.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HBmN!,w_848,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb462a257-e9a4-4957-a17b-b3e3c70f8b15_632x163.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HBmN!,w_1272,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb462a257-e9a4-4957-a17b-b3e3c70f8b15_632x163.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HBmN!,w_1456,c_limit,f_webp,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb462a257-e9a4-4957-a17b-b3e3c70f8b15_632x163.png 1456w\" sizes=\"auto, 100vw\"><img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HBmN!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb462a257-e9a4-4957-a17b-b3e3c70f8b15_632x163.png\" width=\"632\" height=\"163\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;src&quot;:&quot;https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/b462a257-e9a4-4957-a17b-b3e3c70f8b15_632x163.png&quot;,&quot;srcNoWatermark&quot;:null,&quot;fullscreen&quot;:null,&quot;imageSize&quot;:null,&quot;height&quot;:163,&quot;width&quot;:632,&quot;resizeWidth&quot;:null,&quot;bytes&quot;:43168,&quot;alt&quot;:null,&quot;title&quot;:null,&quot;type&quot;:&quot;image/png&quot;,&quot;href&quot;:null,&quot;belowTheFold&quot;:true,&quot;topImage&quot;:false,&quot;internalRedirect&quot;:&quot;https://tjstocks.substack.com/i/221146595?img=https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb462a257-e9a4-4957-a17b-b3e3c70f8b15_632x163.png&quot;,&quot;isProcessing&quot;:false,&quot;align&quot;:null,&quot;offset&quot;:false}\" class=\"sizing-normal\" alt=\"\" srcset=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HBmN!,w_424,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb462a257-e9a4-4957-a17b-b3e3c70f8b15_632x163.png 424w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HBmN!,w_848,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb462a257-e9a4-4957-a17b-b3e3c70f8b15_632x163.png 848w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HBmN!,w_1272,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb462a257-e9a4-4957-a17b-b3e3c70f8b15_632x163.png 1272w, https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!HBmN!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2Fb462a257-e9a4-4957-a17b-b3e3c70f8b15_632x163.png 1456w\" sizes=\"auto, 100vw\" loading=\"lazy\"></picture><div></div></div></div><figcaption class=\"image-caption\">All other variables equal, Tesla has a better chance at a supply squeeze than Advanced Micro Devices. </figcaption></figure></div><p>Again, there are many variables that goes into deciding whether a stock will go up or down. But the point here, it is far more preferable to select stocks where the MASS of insiders, have not dumped off the stock, and this will set you up to have a higher percent chance of a supply squeeze. </p><div><hr></div><p>Normally, I take Monday’s pretty light… seeing how the market digests all of the chaotic news from the weekend. So far, first impressions at market open seem optimistic. Some of the highlights to pay attention to this week:</p><ol><li><p><strong>Earnings:</strong></p><ol><li><p>20 October - SpaceX, <span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;$SPCX&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span> &amp; Netflix, <span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;$NFLX&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span>   </p></li><li><p>21 October - Meta, <span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;$META&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span> &amp; Tesla, <span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;$TSLA&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span> &amp; <span class=\"cashtag-wrap\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;symbol&quot;:&quot;$IBM&quot;}\" data-component-name=\"CashtagToDOM\"></span>     </p></li></ol></li><li><p><strong>Consumer Spending &amp; Credit Reports </strong></p><ol><li><p>Capital One (Tuesday) &amp; American Express (Friday) report updates on credit card delinquency rates and consumer purchasing patterns. </p></li></ol></li><li><p><strong>Housing and Macro Data</strong></p><ol><li><p>September Housing Starts and Pending Home Sales (Tuesday)</p></li></ol></li></ol><p>These are events to watch, but my speculation is they will not be incredibly impactful. I will remind you: the trend remains up, despite the chop. Stay long until proven wrong. </p><div><hr></div><p>If you are looking for stocks to buy or consider, click the links below:</p><h4><strong>→ <a href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/i-reviewed-every-stock-we-own-heres?r=4z8lgl\">A Review of all My Stocks (Click here)</a></strong></h4><ul><li><p>This review of all my current stocks remains applicable, and many remain in buy territory. Feel free to ping me in the main chat if you have any questions. </p></li></ul><h4><strong>→ <a href=\"https://tjstocks.substack.com/p/the-stocktok-summary?r=4z8lgl\">The StockTok Summary Page</a></strong></h4><ul><li><p>This page is updated regularly with my buys, sells, entry targets, exit points. It also contains the regularly updated stocks that meet my buy criteria, the StockTok Screener. This screener goes through 8000+ stocks, and finds the ones that have broken out of consolidations, with institutional volume. I also annotate, which of the 5 is my favorite, when we have results. </p><div><hr></div></li></ul><p>Have a great day, and again, if you have questions, just swing by the main chat and tag me! </p><h4><strong>If you like this content, please like ❤️ and re-stack 🔄, it really helps and only takes a second</strong></h4><div class=\"community-chat\" data-attrs=\"{&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://open.substack.com/pub/tjstocks/chat?utm_source=chat_embed&quot;,&quot;subdomain&quot;:&quot;tjstocks&quot;,&quot;pub&quot;:{&quot;id&quot;:3537822,&quot;name&quot;:&quot;Timothy’s StockTok&quot;,&quot;author_name&quot;:&quot;StockTok 📈&quot;,&quot;author_photo_url&quot;:&quot;https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/$s_!W3S9!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F8add7fc9-8edc-4748-ba33-360428e75ee1_1206x1206.png&quot;}}\" data-component-name=\"CommunityChatRenderPlaceholder\"></div><p></p>",
